# `#538` PASS 2 -- the dedicated adversarial job: equivalence of candidate variants, a premise audit, the cell map

    VERDICT: CLOSES | DOES NOT CLOSE -- <one line naming the deciding item>

**Put the verdict line first.**  The tree under review is `GXEMUL-SEC/` at its current HEAD plus a working-tree change
to `regress/lca_widewrite_probe.py` (the detector) and a comment-only change to `regress/lca_isalane_probe.py`.  No
product line changes.  Ignore any other `src/` under the project root: those copies are pristine 2021 upstream.

**ONE MORE THING IN THE WORKING TREE, AND IT IS NOT THIS ROUND:** `src/devices/dev_lca.c` also carries an UNRELATED, UNCOMMITTED fix from round `#540` -- `CACHE_NONE` -> `CACHE_NONE | PHYSICAL` on the two nested `cpu->memory_rw` forwards in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)`, plus its comment.  It changes the forward's ADDRESS CLASS (physical, not virtual) and nothing about `ofs`, `len` or the write arm's `data[ofs]`.  Every measurement in TABLE.out was taken on 8bd97e4's dev_lca.c, before that edit.  Review THIS diff; ignore the `PHYSICAL` tokens.

**Read ONLY these files. Do not browse anything else:**

    GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c                    DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)
    GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/memory.c                        store_buf()
    GXEMUL-SEC/regress/lca_widewrite_probe.py           the detector under review (4 cells, 13 rows)
    GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/lcalenzerodrop/closure538_20260918/PRETABLE.out
    GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/lcalenzerodrop/closure538_20260918/logs/TABLE.out

**Context.**  `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)` computes `ofs = (relative_addr & 3) % len`.  Its write arm forwards
`byte = data[ofs]` to `LCA_ISA_BASE + relative_addr`.  The PROM GETENV callback is the only guest producer of an
access wider than 8 bytes: it copies a host string with `store_buf()` in chunks of 1024, 256, 64, 16, 4 and 1 bytes,
each chunk only at an address aligned to its size.

The ruled floor is {write arm} x {lane 0, 1, 2, 3} at chunk width 16.  The detector drives one 16-byte chunk per
lane, one isolated emulator session per cell.  Its kill table, 17 legs, matched every prediction (TABLE.out).

## TASK 1 -- EQUIVALENCE, candidate by candidate

For each candidate edit to `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)` below, say whether the detector's 13 rows can tell it from the
shipped handler.  Answer **SEEN** (name the red row) or **UNSEEN**.  For every UNSEEN one, say whether it lies INSIDE
the ruled floor (a breach) or in one of the header's disclosed classes (i)-(viii), and name which class.

    (a)  write arm guarded `&& (len <= 8 || (relative_addr & 3) != 1 || (relative_addr & 0x10))`
    (b)  write arm guarded `&& (len <= 8 || relative_addr != 0x21)`
    (c)  `byte = data[ofs]` -> `byte = data[len > 8 ? (ofs ^ 1) : ofs]`
    (d)  `byte = data[ofs]` -> `byte = data[len > 8 ? 3 - ofs : ofs]`
    (e)  write arm guarded `&& (len != 16)`
    (f)  write arm guarded `&& (len <= 8 || len >= 64)`
    (g)  `ofs = (relative_addr & 3) % len` -> `ofs = (relative_addr & 3) % (len > 8 ? 4 : len)`
    (h)  the forward's length argument `1` -> `len > 8 ? 2 : 1`

## TASK 2 -- PREMISE AUDIT, with file:line for each

Mark each premise TRUE, FALSE or UNSETTLED-FROM-THESE-FILES, and cite the line that settles it:

    P1  store_buf emits a 16-byte chunk only at a 16-aligned guest address, and the whole chunk reaches the handler
        as ONE access of len 16.
    P2  for a 16-byte chunk at k = 0, ofs = (port & 3) % 16 = port & 3.
    P3  a read-arm fall-through of a wide WRITE (the declined case) writes into store_buf's SOURCE buffer.
    P4  each of the four cells' presets differs from its WANT, so a declined write keeps the preset and reds its row.
    P5  the MSR cell reads back OR 0xb0, and the probe applies that transform to BOTH preset and want.

## TASK 3 -- THE CELL MAP

For each of the four floor cells -- lanes 0, 1, 2 and 3 at C = 16 -- name the probe row that pins it, the variant
in TABLE.out that proves the row can go red, and the register value TABLE.out's red run recorded.  Give your
closing count as `<cells pinned> / 4`, with the denominator.

**If you found anything else while verifying a claim, say so briefly.**
