1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """lca_widewrite_probe.py -- #530's width row, CLASS-CLOSED by #538: the four C=16 WRITE lanes.
3: 
4: WHAT IT PINS.  `#530`'s instruction-driven detector, lca_isalane_probe.py, cannot express an access wider than 8 bytes:
5: the widest Alpha store, STQ, is 8.  The only guest producer of a wider access to DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa) is the PROM
6: GETENV callback (CALL_PAL 0x3fffffe), which copies a host string into guest memory with store_buf() -- chunks of
7: 1024/256/64/16/4/1 bytes, each only at an address aligned to its size, each reaching the handler whole.  This file drives
8: that producer at FOUR cells, one per byte lane, ONE ISOLATED EMULATOR SESSION PER CELL: a variant that drops a wide store
9: into the read arm writes zeros into store_buf's SOURCE (the emulator's own boot string), so cells sharing a session would
10: see a shorter string -- one session each removes the ordering question entirely.
11: 
12: HISTORY, because the first version's claim was wrong.  #530 (8bd97e4) shipped ONE cell, (C=16, k=0, lane 3), and said
13: "any guard that declines a len > 8 WRITE" was caught.  Its pass 2 measured seven one-edit variants that pass that cell
14: (regress/artifacts/lcalenzerodrop/opus_p2_20260918/, 102 legs), and the flagship ruled (#530 AF2, fable5 R1/R2) that ONE of
15: them is a floor breach: `&& (len <= 8 || (P & 3) == 3)` services wide writes at the rowed lane only.  LANE is a floor axis
16: because the body's `data[ofs]' distinguishes all four lanes; so the floor is {write arm} x {lane 0, 1, 2, 3}, and #538
17: rows the other three.  Row demand is per LANE, not per variant: the lane-1 exemption `&& (len <= 8 || (P & 3) != 1)`,
18: which the popular two-cell covering {mc2, kbc1024} misses, is red here at `low16'.
19: 
20: CONTRACT (clause e).  DESIGNED TO CATCH, at each of the four byte lanes (C=16, k=0): any variant that DECLINES, REFUSES
21: or MISROUTES a len > 8 WRITE -- the guard form (`len == 0 || len > 8'), the write-arm-conjunct form (`&& len <= 8'), a
22: LANE-conditioned form (`&& (len <= 8 || (P & 3) == L)', or `!= L', for any lane L), and a wrong lane byte (`data[0]'
23: for `data[ofs]', red at lanes 1-3).
24: DISCLOSED, NOT CAUGHT -- each with its warrant, and the named classes are ALREADY RULED in the parent's header:
25:   (i)    width thresholds above 16 (`len <= 16', `<= 64', `<= 256'): the body tests `len' only against 0 (joint cells);
26:          each is MEASURED killed at a wider cell in opus_p2_20260918 (va, vb, vw64, vw256), not rowed here.
27:   (ii)   port-conditioned refusals: the parent's p_port10 class -- the body never compares the port to a constant.  A
28:          refusal below port 0x200 happens to red `low16' (port 0x21); that is incidental, not a contract claim.
29:   (iii)  the discarded sparse bits a<4:0> (k): the parent's lcaisasize class -- a k-keyed or alignment-keyed refusal.
30:   (iv)   chunk position >= 2 of a multi-chunk write: the handler holds no state across calls.
31:   (v)    the READ direction: no wide-read producer exists (store_buf only writes; PROM PUTS reads single bytes).
32:   (vi)   delivery of a wide chunk's NON-LANE bytes: `lcawidefold' (reopened; the drop count is alignment-dependent).
33:   (vii)  data values: a wide chunk never forwards 0 -- argv strings and basenames carry no NUL, and the lane byte sits at
34:          offset <= 3 while the terminator is at >= 15.
35:   (viii) forward COUNT: every row here reads a LATCH, so a len > 8-gated duplicate or added forward is invisible.
36: 
37: WANT IS DERIVED, NEVER TYPED: sim_store_buf() replays src/core/memory.c's store_buf chunking on (a2, len) and applies the
38: SHIPPED handler rule (byte = s[chunk offset + (P & 3) % C], forwarded to port P) to every chunk; the last byte landing on
39: a register's port is that register's WANT.  THE WIDTH IS PINNED BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT BY VALUE: no forwarded byte can
40: distinguish a 16-byte chunk from a 4-byte one at the same address (both forward s[lane]), so each cell declares its chunk
41: list and the probe asserts it -- and asserts that the chunk landing on each observed register is wider than 8.
42: 
43: HARNESS RULES, each from a defect of the first version:
44:   * a session is RETRIED once, with tripled patience, only if its prints are missing AND the emulator was still ALIVE --
45:     as the parent's dsession() does; the first version retried a DEAD session and so could record a host death as a pass.
46:   * exit status is 0 only at full marks; the first version exited 0 on FAIL.
47:   * the last row is an IDENTITY row pinning the row count this file emits.
48: 
49: WITNESS vs DETECTOR.  This is a DETECTOR (green once the defect is gone).  #530's rung-3 WITNESS is lca_isalane_probe.py's
50: 13/16 on the pre-fix build.
51: 
52: MEASURED 2026-09-18 -- #538's kill table, 17 legs, one isolated session per cell; every prediction was written first,
53: in PRETABLE.out, whose mtime predates the frozen instrument.  Logs: regress/artifacts/lcalenzerodrop/closure538_20260918/
54: logs/TABLE.out.  The instrument that ran is that directory's lca_widewrite.frozen.py; this file differs from it ONLY by
55: this paragraph (`diff' the two).
56:     base 13/13     M2_len8 9/13   KILLLEN8 9/13   vc 10/13      vf 10/13
57:     vc_ne0 12/13 (l0w16)   vc_ne1 12/13 (low16)   vc_ne2 12/13 (l2w16)   vc_ne3 12/13 (wide)
58:     ve 12/13 (low16 -- INCIDENTAL, disclosed class (ii))
59:     va vb vg vt1 vt2 13/13 (disclosed (i), (iii), (iv))     vd vh 13/13 (EQUIVALENT)
60:   17 of 17 as predicted, red-row sets included.  The lane-1 exemption that the covering {mc2, kbc1024} misses is red
61:   at `low16' (vc_ne1).
62: """
63: import os, pty, re, select, sys, time
64: 
65: BIN   = sys.argv[1]
66: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"
67: MACH  = "alphabook1"
68: DUMMY = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "alpha_dummy.bin")
69: 
70: # ---- encoder, copied from the parent via the first version, unchanged
71: ZERO, T0, T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6, T7 = 31, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8
72: A0, A1, A2, A3 = 16, 17, 18, 19
73: RA = 26
74: def mem(op, ra, rb, disp):
75:     assert -32768 <= disp <= 32767, "displacement %d out of range" % disp
76:     return (op << 26) | (ra << 21) | (rb << 16) | (disp & 0xffff)
77: def LDA (ra, disp, rb=ZERO): return mem(0x08, ra, rb, disp)
78: def LDAH(ra, disp, rb=ZERO): return mem(0x09, ra, rb, disp)
79: def LDBU(ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x0a, ra, rb, disp)
80: def STB (ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x0e, ra, rb, disp)
81: def LDQ (ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x29, ra, rb, disp)
82: CALL_PAL_PROM = (0x00 << 26) | 0x3fffffe
83: 
84: def load_const(reg, val):
85:     lo = val & 0xffff
86:     hi = (val >> 16) & 0xffff
87:     if lo >= 0x8000:
88:         hi = (hi + 1) & 0xffff
89:     ops = [LDAH(reg, hi if hi < 0x8000 else hi - 0x10000)]
90:     if lo:
91:         ops.append(LDA(reg, lo if lo < 0x8000 else lo - 0x10000, reg))
92:     return ops
93: 
94: SENT = 0x0bad1d8a
95: def sent(reg): return load_const(reg, SENT)
96: 
97: K0SEG        = 0xfffffc0000000000
98: def k0(p):   return K0SEG | p
99: LCA_PCI_SIO  = 0x1c0000000
100: LCA_ISA_BASE = LCA_PCI_SIO + 0x10000000
101: def SP(port):   return LCA_PCI_SIO + (port << 5)
102: def FLAT(port): return LCA_ISA_BASE + port
103: SCRATCH, CODE = 0x01020000, 0x01040000
104: KBC_CMD, KBC_DAT = 0x64, 0x60
105: 
106: def session(bootstr, cmds, settle, spin):
107:     pid, fd = pty.fork()
108:     if pid == 0:
109:         os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-x", "-E", "alpha", "-e", MACH, "-M", "64",
110:                        "-o", bootstr, "0x20000000:" + DUMMY])
111:         os._exit(127)
112:     buf = ""
113:     def rd(t):
114:         nonlocal buf
115:         end = time.time() + t
116:         while time.time() < end:
117:             r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.1)
118:             if not r:
119:                 continue
120:             try:
121:                 d = os.read(fd, 65536)
122:                 if not d:
123:                     return False
124:                 buf += d.decode("latin-1", "replace")
125:             except OSError:
126:                 return False
127:         return True
128:     alive = rd(settle)
129:     for i, c in enumerate(cmds):
130:         try:
131:             os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode("latin-1"))
132:         except OSError:
133:             alive = False; break
134:         if not rd(spin if i == len(cmds) - 1 else 0.45):
135:             alive = False; break
136:     try:
137:         os.write(fd, b"quit\n"); rd(0.5)
138:     except OSError:
139:         pass
140:     try:
141:         os.close(fd)
142:     except OSError:
143:         pass
144:     try:
145:         os.waitpid(pid, 0)
146:     except OSError:
147:         pass
148:     return buf.replace("\r", ""), alive
149: 
150: def build(consts, phases):
151:     prog = load_const(T0, SCRATCH)
152:     lens = [len(prog)]
153:     for ops, _ in phases:
154:         prog += ops
155:         lens.append(len(ops))
156:     cmds  = ["put d 0x%x, 0x%x" % (SCRATCH + 8 * i, v) for i, v in enumerate(consts)]
157:     cmds += ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (k0(CODE) + 4 * i, op) for i, op in enumerate(prog)]
158:     cmds += ["pc=0x%x" % k0(CODE), "step %d" % lens[0]]
159:     for (ops, pr), n in zip(phases, lens[1:]):
160:         cmds.append("step %d" % n)
161:         if pr is not None:
162:             cmds.append("print %s" % pr)
163:     return cmds
164: 
165: def printed(t, reg):
166:     m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
167:     return None if not m else int(m.group(1), 16)
168: 
169: rows = []
170: def row(name, got, want, note=""):
171:     assert len(name) <= 13, "row name %r exceeds 13 characters (the %%-14s column + gate pattern)" % name
172:     ok = (got == want)
173:     rows.append((name, ok))
174:     g = got if not isinstance(got, int) else "0x%x" % got
175:     w = want if not isinstance(want, int) else "0x%x" % want
176:     print("%-14s %-24s %-24s %-56s %s" % (name, g, w, note, "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
177:     return ok
178: 
179: # ---- the producer, replayed (src/core/memory.c store_buf) + the SHIPPED lca_isa write rule
180: def sim_store_buf(a, n):
181:     out, off, psize = [], 0, 1024
182:     while n != 0:
183:         if (a & (psize - 1)) == 0:
184:             while n >= psize:
185:                 out.append((a, psize, off)); a += psize; off += psize; n -= psize
186:         psize >>= 2
187:     return out                                # the trailing store_byte loop is dead: psize 1 drains it
188: 
189: def shipped_lands(a_sparse, n, sbytes):
190:     return [((a >> 5), sbytes[off + ((a >> 5) & 3) % c]) for a, c, off in sim_store_buf(a_sparse, n)]
191: 
192: ALPH = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_"
193: def pat(n): return (ALPH * (n // len(ALPH) + 1))[:n]
194: IDENT = lambda v: v
195: MSRX  = lambda v: v | 0xb0                    # the ns16550 MSR reads back OR DCD|DSR|CTS
196: 
197: #  ---- THE CELLS
198: #  name: (a3, target port, k, -o string, chunks expected, [(reg port, kind, preset, xform, row tag)])
199: #  THE FLOOR, as ruled (fable5, #530 AF2, R1/R2): the four C=16 WRITE lanes at k = 0.  `wide' is the shipped
200: #  cell and keeps its row names; the other three close the LANE partition that `data[ofs]' distinguishes.
201: #  Each a3 = 16 against a 16-character string, so len = min(16, 17) = 16: ONE 16-byte chunk (asserted below).
202: #  name     a3  port   k  -o string            chunks  [(reg port, kind, preset, xform, row tag)]
203: CELLS = {
204:     "wide":  (16, 0x2ff, 0, "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP", [16], [(0x2ff, "sp", 0x5a, IDENT, "")]),  # lane 3: ns16550 SCR
205:     "l0w16": (16, 0x2fc, 0, "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP", [16], [(0x2fc, "sp", 0x03, IDENT, "")]),  # lane 0: ns16550 MCR
206:     "low16": (16, 0x021, 0, "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP", [16], [(0x021, "sp", 0xff, IDENT, "")]),  # lane 1: 8259 IMR
207:     "l2w16": (16, 0x2fe, 0, "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP", [16], [(0x2fe, "sp", 0x00, MSRX,  "")]),  # lane 2: ns16550 MSR
208: }
209: assert sorted(spec[1] & 3 for spec in CELLS.values()) == [0, 1, 2, 3], "the floor is ALL FOUR lanes"
210: 
211: def run_cell(name, spec):
212:     a3v, tgt, k, bootstr, chunks, regs = spec
213:     sbytes = bootstr.encode("latin-1") + b"\0"
214:     lenv = a3v if len(bootstr) >= a3v else len(bootstr) + 1   # alpha_prom_call: min(a3, strlen + 1)
215:     a_sparse = (tgt << 5) + k
216:     got_chunks = [c for _, c, _ in sim_store_buf(a_sparse, lenv)]
217:     assert got_chunks == chunks, "cell %s: replayed chunks %r != declared %r -- the WIDTH is not what this cell claims" \
218:         % (name, got_chunks, chunks)
219:     lands = shipped_lands(a_sparse, lenv, sbytes)
220:     #  THE WIDTH PIN (fable5 R2; the #530 pass-2 F10 gap).  No forwarded-byte VALUE can pin the width: a 4-byte chunk
221:     #  at the same address forwards the same s[lane].  So the construction itself is asserted: the chunk that lands on
222:     #  each observed register must be WIDER THAN 8, or this cell is not testing what its rows claim.
223:     for a, c, off in sim_store_buf(a_sparse, lenv):
224:         if any((a >> 5) == port for port, _, _, _, _ in regs):
225:             assert c > 8, "cell %s: the chunk landing on port 0x%x is %d bytes -- not a wide write" % (name, a >> 5, c)
226:     consts = [0, k0(SP(tgt) + k)]
227:     def slot(v):
228:         consts.append(v); return 8 * (len(consts) - 1)
229:     res = [T3, T4, T5, T6, T7]
230:     rname = {T3: "t3", T4: "t4", T5: "t5", T6: "t6", T7: "t7"}
231:     plan = []
232:     for port, kind, preset, xf, tag in regs:
233:         if kind == "sp":
234:             s_reg = slot(k0(SP(port)))
235:             pre = [LDQ(T2, s_reg, T0)] + load_const(T1, preset) + [STB(T1, 0, T2)]
236:             rd_ = lambda r, s_reg=s_reg: [LDQ(T2, s_reg, T0)] + sent(r) + [LDBU(r, 0, T2)]
237:             arm = []
238:         else:                                 # the 8042 command byte, sequenced through FLAT
239:             s_cmd, s_dat = slot(k0(FLAT(KBC_CMD))), slot(k0(FLAT(KBC_DAT)))
240:             pre = ([LDQ(T2, s_cmd, T0)] + load_const(T1, 0x60) + [STB(T1, 0, T2)]
241:                    + [LDQ(T2, s_dat, T0)] + load_const(T1, preset) + [STB(T1, 0, T2)])
242:             rd_ = lambda r, s_cmd=s_cmd, s_dat=s_dat: ([LDQ(T2, s_cmd, T0)] + load_const(T1, 0x20)
243:                    + [STB(T1, 0, T2), LDQ(T2, s_dat, T0)] + sent(r) + [LDBU(r, 0, T2)])
244:             arm = [LDQ(T2, s_cmd, T0)] + load_const(T1, 0x60) + [STB(T1, 0, T2)]
245:         want = preset
246:         for p, b in lands:
247:             if p == port:
248:                 want = b
249:         plan.append((port, xf, preset, tag, pre, rd_, arm, want))
250:     phases = [(pre, None) for _, _, _, _, pre, _, _, _ in plan]
251:     phases += [(rd_(res[j]), rname[res[j]]) for j, (_, _, _, _, _, rd_, _, _) in enumerate(plan)]
252:     arm_all = sum((arm for _, _, _, _, _, _, arm, _ in plan), [])
253:     phases.append((arm_all + load_const(A0, 0x22) + load_const(A1, 0x8) + [LDQ(A2, 8, T0)]
254:                    + load_const(A3, a3v) + [LDQ(RA, 0, T0), CALL_PAL_PROM], None))
255:     n = len(plan)
256:     phases += [(rd_(res[n + j]), rname[res[n + j]]) for j, (_, _, _, _, _, rd_, _, _) in enumerate(plan)]
257:     consts[0] = k0(CODE) + 4 * (len(load_const(T0, SCRATCH)) + sum(len(o) for o, _ in phases[:2 * n + 1]))
258:     cmds = build(consts, phases)
259:     names = [rname[r] for r in res[:2 * n]]
260:     txt, alive = session(bootstr, cmds, 3.0, 4.0)
261:     retried = False
262:     if alive and any(printed(txt, x) is None for x in names):   # F6: never retry a session that DIED
263:         retried = True
264:         txt, alive = session(bootstr, cmds, 9.0, 12.0)
265:     print("  cell %-8s a3=%d len=%d a2=SP(0x%x)+%d chunks=%s retried=%s"
266:           % (name, a3v, lenv, tgt, k, got_chunks, "yes" if retried else "none"))
267:     if os.environ.get("WIDEWRITE_RAW"):
268:         open(os.environ["WIDEWRITE_RAW"] + "." + name, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(txt)
269:     row("%s alive" % name, "alive" if alive else "died", "alive",
270:         "the guest survives the inline CALL_PAL 0x3fffffe")
271:     for j, (port, xf, preset, tag, _, _, _, want) in enumerate(plan):
272:         row(("%s live%s" % (name, tag)).strip(), printed(txt, rname[res[j]]), xf(preset),
273:             "ROUND-TRIP CONTROL: preset 0x%02x round-trips through port 0x%x" % (preset, port))
274:     for j, (port, xf, preset, tag, _, _, _, want) in enumerate(plan):
275:         row(("%s getenv%s" % (name, tag)).strip(), printed(txt, rname[res[n + j]]), xf(want),
276:             "len %d: the shipped rule puts 0x%02x on port 0x%x" % (lenv, want, port))
277: 
278: print("lca_widewrite -- binary=%s label=%s machine=%s cells=%s" % (BIN, LABEL, MACH, " ".join(CELLS)))
279: for name, spec in CELLS.items():
280:     run_cell(name, spec)
281: EXPECT_ROWS = 3 * len(CELLS) + 1               # alive, live, getenv per cell, plus this row
282: row("row count", len(rows) + 1, EXPECT_ROWS, "IDENTITY: the row count this file emits")
283: ok = sum(1 for _, o in rows if o)
284: print("WIDEWRITE_RESULT=%d/%d" % (ok, len(rows)))
285: print("WIDEWRITE_DONE")
286: sys.exit(0 if ok == len(rows) else 1)

